id: ops-minimal-witnesses
title: Reduce diagnostic failures to minimal shared input witnesses
description: Read-only reduction of explicit sufficient input facts and canonical diagnostic command references into compact shared witnesses.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:26:50.089Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T23:38:41.757Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Five failures caused by one incompatible SDK produce one common witness plus five affected checks; unrelated failures stay separate; reduction never upgrades an unverified diagnosis into a proven root cause.; Typed SDK and CLI, strict bounded input and finite output, TOON/JSON, remedies, non-git public tracker validation and npm/Bun CI release gates."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:26:55.146Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current CLI 2026.10.25 and public sibling source/docs. CLI owns complete reads, status roles, output rendering and budgets; pm-ops diagnostic-plans owns bounded canonical probes, evidence-expiry owns retained claim freshness. pm-context checks contradictory claims, pm-lint criterion evidence, pm-observer repeated actions, pm-hypothesis competing explanations. None minimizes sufficient explicit diagnostic input sets. Reuse diagnostic command identities and host TOON/JSON; add a stateless reducer with no tracker writes, import/sync, leases, journal or status interpretation. Exact minimum means fewest distinct retained facts among declared sufficient clauses; deterministic ties. Group only equal class, scope, command, diagnosis and chosen fact set. No root-cause proof is inferred."
  "2026-10-25T23:35:40.939Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses an exact bounded set search over declared sufficient clauses. Refinement: checks with different canonical probe commands may share one witness when class, scope, diagnosis and chosen facts match; each affected check retains its own command. Five SDK mismatch checks now span schema/items/history probes. Different failure classes/scopes/diagnoses stay separate. Source-only negative controls bypassed minimization and grouping independently: acceptance failed with 3 retained facts instead of 2, and 1 affected check instead of 5; original source restored byte-for-byte. First complete targeted run: 7 tests passed and reducer coverage 100/100/100/100. Seeded model: 500 sequences, 8 operations each, old-input replay and JSON/TOON/CRLF variants; every sequence reads native records and relationships back through the SDK and verifies reducer byte identity before SDK cache reads. No native import/export/sync or shared-state transition exists in this feature."
  "2026-10-25T23:37:51.745Z",codex-agent,"Final focused suite passed through pinned pm test --run --progress: 7 tests, 0 failed/skipped; 500 seeded sequences of 8 operations. Typecheck, lint, docstrings (320 declarations) and duplication (0 percent, unchanged zero threshold) pass. Public main snapshot 11607ad: read-only non-git copy, 318 files, 11 schema types, 155 items, 2104 history entries verified. Six controlled canonical budget failures produce 2 witnesses retaining 6 checks (5 common); 3 distinct facts retained. Expanded JSON 2024 bytes, input selection 1262 bytes, reduced JSON 931 bytes, TOON 797 bytes; repeat output identical and every tracker byte unchanged. These are controlled process/network budget failures, not a public SDK defect. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI because the shared host is saturated. Linked-test recording is disabled by tracker policy, so this comment retains the successful result without changing that policy. No pm CLI/SDK defect was encountered."
